  "worked_solution": "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{y}={\u222c}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is a type I plane region, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/07701125c6acc36d127556bf95940bf0f74ba9ef3072f3af22dac26edc053a74.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 4x}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=x.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={\u222c}_{D}x\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{D}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{4x}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot [y]_{y=0}^{y=4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot 4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
